  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">All three wrappers compile + lint-clean; each ≤~60 LOC.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`SendEmailStep` locks `mount='inline'` and forwards `composerRef` (host calls `composerRef.current.send()`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`SendEmailDialog` locks `mount='dialog'`, owns `open`/`onClose`, and maps engine `onSent`→`props.onSent` + close.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`SendEmailPage` locks `mount='page'`, requires `mode`, maps `onClose`→`onCancel`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All three wrappers + prop interfaces exported through `EmailComposer/index.ts` and the shared-lib barrel.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `@spaarke/auth` import in any wrapper (grep-verified).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build:prod` + `npm run lint` clean in `@spaarke/ui-components`.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Callers import wrappers, not the engine. Direct `&lt;EmailComposer /&gt;` use is reserved for non-standard mounts (side panel/drawer) and requires a justifying comment per design §5.1.2.

    W6 consumers: task 060 (SummarizeFilesDialog/FilePreviewDialog/DocumentEmailWizard) uses `SendEmailDialog`/`SendEmailStep`; task 061 (5 create-record wizards + CreateMatter fork) uses `SendEmailStep`; W4 task 041 mounts `SendEmailPage`.
  </notes>

